<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cornelius Fuscus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 86/87 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cornelius Fuscus was a Roman equestrian who served as praetorian prefect under the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domitian">Domitian</a>. In 86 or 87 CE he led a Roman army across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacia">Dacia</a> to punish King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decebalus">Decebalus</a> for raids into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a>, but he was killed and his army destroyed, possibly at Tapae. The defeat led to further Roman campaigns against Dacia.</p></div>
